{"kind":"request","text":"S4 has a concrete source gap for the explanatory retirement conflict reply.\n\nThe control row stores the fingerprint but no actor. A valid empty or {} retirement body keeps revoke NULL. Even a saved first revoke is one singleton per Agent with no control-op binding, so it cannot identify the original signer for every conflicting operation. I checked the actual control schema, insert/read functions and retirement-body decoder. The current caller and target Agent key supply no substitute fact.\n\nMay S4 add one nullable immutable control.retire_actor column, populated only when the authenticated ORIGINAL retirement inserts its new control row in the same cleanup transaction? Retries, completion and answer expiry never change it. Existing non-retirement rows and legacy rows stay NULL; no backfill or inference from another caller, target key or optional revoke occurs. Existing reservation/accounting and bounds continue covering its bytes.\n\nOnly a fresh definite retired/compromised original key, or removed member for that same known key, may enable your exact next member after current-caller authority and exact owner/clock checks. Unknown/null/unavailable facts and active-key role loss supply no proof. NULL or unproved legacy rows keep the exact existing plain fingerprint 409. The old signer's 403 and every operation/cleanup/replay rule stay unchanged.\n\nThis is local attribution for your response condition, with no ownership mechanism. If legacy rows must always receive the explanation too, the stored source cannot establish the required fact without a separately trusted migration input.\n\nFull plan: /private/tmp/artroom-r3b-design-s4-retire-actor-metadata-feasibility-plan-20261111.md, SHA-256 3c13ed50074e6e3b5ca1dde7f855fbc70f38fea204b1e05c7222eb2a093938a1. I read it fully. No cleanup patch or body has run. The earlier management plan's no-new-proof-field constraint was our proposal, not a prohibition in your ruling.","body":{"conditions":"Rule on one immutable nullable local retire_actor column and plain-409 legacy fallback needed to qualify 63636688's explanatory conflict response. No ownership transfer, replay eligibility, cleanup effect, wire change or deployment.","no_git_artifact":"true","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}